{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 928 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "e6547bb10a6ccec4d55880783dcee3838a2989926c71405a98c135cf01546148" :edb/db-before-t 927 :edb/db-after-t 928 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534240 50 #inst "2026-10-11T18:08:01.619Z" 13194139534240 17592186045417 true] [17592186172056 1038 #edb/ref 17592186415536 13194139534240 17592186045417 true] [17592186172132 1038 #edb/ref 17592186415535 13194139534240 17592186045417 true] [17592186172133 1038 #edb/ref 17592186415537 13194139534240 17592186045417 true] [17592186172233 1068 #edb/ref 17592186168261 13194139534240 17592186045417 false] [17592186172233 1068 #edb/ref 17592186415531 13194139534240 17592186045417 true] [17592186172233 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534240 17592186045417 true] [17592186172233 1071 "$$\n⟨\\text{_______}\\,,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ⟩\n$$\n\nThe fundamental vector product of the surface of revolution generated by rotating the curve $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ by $2\\pi $ radians about the $x$-axis for $x\\in [0,\\pi ]$ is given above. What is the $1$st component of the product?" 13194139534240 17592186045417 true] [17592186172233 1071 "$⟨_______,-\\sin x\\cos θ,-\\sin x\\sin θ⟩$\n\nThe fundamental vector product of the surface of revolution generated by rotating the curve $y = \\sin x$ by $2π$ radians about the $x$-axis for $x ∈ [0, π]$ is given above. What is the $1$st component of the product?" 13194139534240 17592186045417 false] [17592186172233 1074 "Notice that $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in [0,\\pi ].$ The parametrization of our surface of revolution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=⟨x,f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ⟩,\\,(x,\\theta )\\in D\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$ and\n\n$$\nD={(x,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\pi ,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂x},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂x},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂x}⟩=⟨1,\\,{f}^{′}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,{f}^{′}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ⟩ \\\\ {r}_{\\theta }^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂\\theta },\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂\\theta },\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂\\theta }⟩=⟨0,\\,-f\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,f\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{\\theta }^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & {f}^{′}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & {f}^{′}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 0 & -f\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & f\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & {f}^{′}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ -f\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & f\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & {f}^{′}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 0 & f\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & {f}^{′}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 0 & -f\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨f{f}^{′}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +f{f}^{′}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ,\\,-f\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,-f\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ⟩ \\\\  & =⟨f{f}^{′},\\,-f\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,-f\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $f=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$ we obtain ${f}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ So, finally, we conclude that the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{\\theta }^{′}=⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534240 17592186045417 true] [17592186415510 1043 #edb/ref 17592186415538 13194139534240 17592186045417 true] [17592186415510 1043 #edb/ref 17592186415539 13194139534240 17592186045417 true] [17592186415510 1043 #edb/ref 17592186415540 13194139534240 17592186045417 true] [17592186415510 1043 #edb/ref